The paper’s decisive result is not “recover an arbitrary matrix.” Section 4 reduces PARTITION to a very specific spectrum  
\((S/2,S/2,-i_n,\ldots,-i_1)\), and Theorem 5.3 makes a partition into two Suleĭmanova sublists a polynomially checkable witness. I’m evaluating that paper-native certificate instead, because arbitrary rational spectra need not even have known rational matrix witnesses (the paper explicitly leaves that issue open).
