The paper is correctly rejected for this benchmark.

- G and V pass using the paper’s Lemma 4.1 and Theorem 5.4 SP-partition certificate.
- Track A fails because the generated distribution has an O(n) residue decoder.
- Track B fails gated G9(b): all 3 hinted oracles solved n=36, and a hinted oracle also solved n=64 after the single permitted escalation.
- Mechanical and compact-route costs are recorded for both attempted sizes.

Full evidence: [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1608.00931/REJECTED.md)

The relevant definitions and complexity results were verified against the [full arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1608.00931). No shipping README or self-test report was created because the instructions require stopping after the second G9(b) failure.
